    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New component** \u2014 `service/IdempotencyStore.java`: a small, single-responsibility bean that remembers which owner id a given `Idempotency-Key` first created (thread-safe `ConcurrentHashMap`). It ignores blank/absent keys and, via `putIfAbsent`, guarantees the first create wins.\n\n**Controller** \u2014 `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Injected `IdempotencyStore` and `HttpServletRequest` (a request-scoped proxy) so the header can be read without altering the generated `OwnersApi` interface.\n- At the start of `addOwner`, a small private helper `replayCreatedOwner(...)` looks up the key; if it was already used, it returns the originally created owner mapped to a DTO with **200 OK** \u2014 short-circuiting before the duplicate/identity checks that would otherwise return 409.\n- After a successful create, it records `key \u2192 owner id`.\n\nThe helper returns `null` (proceed normally) when there's no key, the key is unseen, or the recorded owner no longer exists \u2014 so ordinary creates and requests without a key are unaffected.\n\nThe idempotency logic lives in its own component and a focused helper rather than bloating `addOwner`, and it reuses the existing `ownerMapper` and `clinicService.findOwnerById`. The acceptance test (`coreIdempotentRepeat`) and the full suite pass.",
