    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is `addOwner(...)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:114-167`, taking a `@Valid OwnerFieldsDto` body.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Security (before the method runs)\n\n1. **Authorization**: `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise `permitAll`).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (triggered by `@Valid`, before the body executes)\n\nField constraints:\n2. **`firstName`** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`\n3. **`lastName`** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`\n4. **`title`** \u2014 `@Pattern(^(MR|MRS|MS|DR)$)` (optional)\n5. **`city`** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..80)`\n6. **`telephone`** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`, `@Size(1..20)`, plus custom **`@Telephone`** (normalizes to E.164 and checks national-number length)\n7. **`email`** \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(1..255)`, plus custom **`@NotDisposableEmail`** (rejects disposable domains)\n8. **`address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`** \u2014 each `@Size(1..255)`\n\nClass-level constraints:\n9. **`@ValidAddress`** \u2014 requires a non-blank `addressLine1` OR `address`\n10. **`@ValidPostcode`** \u2014 validates `postcode` against `city`\n\nA failure here is turned into **400 Bad Request** by `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (`MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler). (No validation groups are used \u2014 all run in the default group.)\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Controller body, in execution order (`addOwner`)\n\n11. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 if `Idempotency-Key` header matches a prior request in the in-memory `IdempotencyStore`, return the original owner with **200 OK** (short-circuits everything below).\n12. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`), which itself performs side-effects:\n    - normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (`TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`)\n    - normalizes `addressLine1/2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE)\n    - composes `address` (prefers normalized address lines, else the flat address)\n13. **Future-date guard** \u2014 `isRegistrationDateInFuture` \u2192 **400** if `registrationDate` is after today.\n14. **Resolve registration date** \u2014 default null \u2192 `LocalDate.now()`, then roll forward off weekends/holidays to next business day.\n15. **Daily limit** \u2014 `isDailyOwnerLimitReached` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests** if \u2265100 owners already registered that day.\n16. **City capacity** \u2014 `isCityAtCapacity` \u2192 **409 Conflict** if \u226550 owners in that city.\n17. **Assign household id** \u2014 deterministic SHA-256 of normalized lastName + postcode (skipped if postcode null).\n18. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 if another (non-deleted) owner shares last name + postcode and client did **not** set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n19. **Identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 `existsOwnerWithIdentityKey` \u2192 **409 Conflict** if a non-deleted owner has the same `telephone|email|householdId`.\n20. **Derived counters set** \u2014 `namesakeCount`, `householdSize`, `bulkSignupWarning` (warning flag when >80 owners that day).\n21. **Possible-duplicate soft match** \u2014 unless declared household member, sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` from a same-lastName+postcode-but-different-telephone lookup.\n22. **Save** (`clinicService.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`), which on save:\n    - generates a `customerCode` if absent (`CustomerCodeGenerator`, deduplicated against existing codes)\n    - **`@PrePersist`** on `Owner` re-defaults `registrationDate` to today + rolls forward to a business day\n    - `Owner.setEmail` lower-cases the email (note: not trimmed)\n    - `em.persist`, IDENTITY-generated id\n    - entity-level constraints enforced on flush (`firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`)\n23. **Audit** \u2014 `ownerAuditor.auditCreated` logs id/customerCode/registrationDate/membership fields to the `\"AUDIT\"` logger.\n24. **Record idempotency** \u2014 store `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 owner id.\n25. **Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (deriving read-only display/membership fields), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- `addOwner` is **not** `@Transactional` at the controller level \u2014 each `clinicService` call is its own transaction, so the pre-save duplicate/limit checks (steps 15-19) are not atomic with the save (step 22), leaving a TOCTOU race window.\n- No emails, notifications, or events are published in the create path; there is no password encoding for owners.\n- The business-day rollforward runs twice (step 14 in the controller and again in `@PrePersist`), and telephone/email normalization is spread across the mapper and entity setters rather than one central step."
